<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KFA seeks 70,000 tonnes of soymeal.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KFA seeks 70,000 tonnes of soymeal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Feed Association (KFA) on Tuesday invited tenders for 70,000 tonnes of soymeal, traders said.  </p>
<p>Traders said shipment was set for January 11-30 if sourced from China, for December 27-January 15 if sourced from India, or for December 1-20 if sourced from South America or the U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p>    POSITION   TONNE	ARRIVAL PORTS</p>
<p>    ONE	 50,000     Inchon, Kunsan, Pusan or Ulsan</p>
<p>    TWO	 20,000     Inchon, Pusan or Ulsan</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
